    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the membership level rule with the specified points system.\n\n**`MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 rewrote to compute points (start at 0; +2 email present; +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`; +2 for a household of 3+ members; +3 for tenure > 365 days), then bucket points into a level (1 for 0\u20131, 2 for 2\u20133, 3 for 4\u20135, 4 for 6+). Exposed as `points(Owner)`, `levelForPoints(int)`, and `of(Owner)` (kept so the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` caller works unchanged).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipPoints` mapping (`MembershipLevel.points(owner)`) alongside the existing `membershipLevel` mapping, so both fields are returned.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema field (0\u20138) and updated the `membershipLevel` description/constraints (now min 1, max 4) to reflect the new bucketing.\n\nThe acceptance test (a fresh owner with an email, no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure \u2192 `membershipPoints=3`, `membershipLevel=2`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
