    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of what happens on `POST /api/owners`, following the pipeline in `owners.POST.yml` step by step. (Every step runs inside one shared `transaction` governance, committed once at the end.)\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n0. **Authorization** \u2014 the whole endpoint requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; otherwise it's rejected before the pipeline runs.\n\n## 1. `ValidateOwnerFields` (validations + body normalization)\nValidations, in this order:\n1. **Registration date not in the future** \u2014 if a `registrationDate` is supplied and later than the server's `LocalDate.now()`, throw `OwnerRegistrationDateFutureException`.\n2. **Required fields** \u2014 collects *every* missing/blank offender among `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (blank *after* normalization), `city`, `telephone`; if any, throw `OwnerFieldsRequiredException` with the full list.\n   - Note: address is normalized first (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`) and counted as missing when it collapses to empty.\n3. **Postcode** (optional) \u2014 via `OwnerPostcode.validate`: if present must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (`Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099`) must fall in that range; else `OwnerPostcodeInvalidException`. A city with no known region accepts any 4-digit code.\n\nSide-effects (mutations written back onto the request body, then published for later steps):\n4. **Address** set to its normalized form.\n5. **Telephone** normalized to E.164 (`OwnerTelephone.toE164`: strip spaces/dashes/brackets; default country code `+61` dropping a leading `0`; must be 8\u201315 digits; `+61`\u21d29 national digits, `+1`\u21d210) \u2014 else `OwnerTelephoneInvalidException`.\n6. **Email** (optional) normalized (`OwnerEmail.normalize`: trimmed, lower-cased); if non-blank must match the email syntax pattern (else `OwnerEmailInvalidException`) and its domain must not be on the disposable blocklist `mailinator.com`/`tempmail.com`/`guerrillamail.com` (else `OwnerEmailDisposableException`). Null when omitted.\n\n## 2. `CheckOwnerDailyLimit` (validation)\n7. Compute the effective **business day** (supplied date or today, rolled forward off weekends to Monday). Count existing owners with that `registrationDate`; if **\u2265 100**, throw `OwnerDailyLimitException` (429).\n\n## 3. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` (validation)\n8. Count existing owners in the same `city` (case-insensitive); if **\u2265 50**, throw `OwnerCityCapacityException` (409).\n\n## 4. `BuildOwner` (side-effect: create the entity)\n9. Map the DTO to an `Owner` entity; default `registrationDate` to today if omitted, then **roll it forward to the next business day** (weekend \u2192 Monday).\n\n## 5. `AssignHousehold` (side-effect)\n10. Compute and set a deterministic **`householdId`** = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalize(lastName) + \"|\" + postcode`.\n\n## 6. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` (validation)\n11. Unless the request flag `sharesHousehold` is true (which bypasses this), scan existing owners; if any already has the same `householdId`, throw `OwnerIdentityConflictException` (409).\n\n## 7. `AssignPossibleDuplicate` (side-effect: soft-duplicate flagging)\n12. Set `possibleDuplicate=false` / `possibleDuplicateOf=null`. If not a declared household member and a postcode is present, scan for an existing owner with same `lastName` (case-insensitive) + same `postcode` but *different* `telephone`; if found, set `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = the matching owner's id (lowest id when several match). Owner is still created either way.\n\n## 8. `AssignHouseholdSize` (side-effect)\n13. Set **`householdMemberCount`** = existing owners sharing the `householdId` **+ 1** (the new owner).\n\n## 9. `AssignCustomerCode` (side-effect)\n14. Set **`customerCode`** = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where REGION comes from the owner's postcode range (`NSW/VIC/QLD/UNKNOWN`) and HASH8 = first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n## 10. `AssignNamesakeCount` (side-effect)\n15. Set **`namesakeCount`** = number of existing owners sharing `firstName` + `lastName` (case-insensitive; excludes the new owner).\n\n## 11. `AssignBulkSignupWarning` (side-effect)\n16. Set **`bulkSignupWarning`** = true if **> 80** existing owners already exist for this owner's business day (else false).\n\n## 12. `SaveOwner` (side-effect: persistence)\n17. `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 persists the entity and assigns its generated id.\n\n## 13. `AuditOwnerCreated` (side-effect: logging)\n18. Emit an `AUDIT` log line with the new owner's `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and computed `membershipLevel`.\n\n## 14. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (side-effect: response)\n19. Map to `OwnerDto` and send **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body.\n\n---\n\nTwo things worth flagging as you read this:\n- The **daily limit (\u2265100)** and **city capacity (\u226550)** are checked *before* `BuildOwner`, so they count against the request's raw values, while the later `bulkSignupWarning` counts against the entity's already-adjusted business day \u2014 consistent by design, per the doc comments.\n- All the count-based steps (daily limit, city capacity, identity uniqueness, household size, namesake, bulk warning) iterate `ownerRepository.findAll()` and run *before* the save, so none of them sees the new owner itself."
